  "6": [
    ["Determination of wages, special payments and allowances", "The Company determines wages, overtime pay, holiday work pay and holiday overtime pay by considering qualifications, responsibilities, workload, nature and quality of work. Work of equal value will be paid at an equal rate regardless of gender and whether the employee is paid daily or monthly, at a rate the Company considers appropriate.", "The Company may provide a temporary special payment or allowance when an employee is assigned outside the employee's regular unit, passes training or testing that improves work efficiency, or assumes greater responsibility than employees at the same level. The amount and period will follow the agreement or Company determination. A special payment or allowance is not wages and is not included in the overtime calculation. It will normally be paid with wages in the regular payroll cycle.", "Special payments are treated as other payments and are not a wage base for calculations under applicable labour laws, subject to Company procedures."],
