  "7": [
    ["Work is divided into two categories."],
    ["Onshore work.", "Normal work is six days per week, Monday through Saturday.", "Normal working hours are 08:00 to 17:00.", "The rest period is 12:00 to 13:00.", "The Company may agree in advance to different rest periods when appropriate, but total rest time must never exceed two hours per day. Rest time exceeding two hours will be treated as normal working time during which no work was actually performed.", "Shift work is divided into two shifts.", "Shift 1: normal working hours are 08:00 to 17:00, with a rest period from 12:00 to 13:00.", "Shift 2: normal working hours are 18:00 to 03:00, with a rest period from 22:00 to 23:00.", "The Company may set different start and finish times, provided total normal working hours do not exceed 48 hours per week."],
    ["Offshore work: consecutive work periods are set by agreement, but may not exceed 28 consecutive days. Normal work is 12 hours per day, with agreed start and finish times not exceeding 12 hours in one day.", "There are two rest periods per workday: one hour after four hours of work and 15 minutes after eight hours of work."],
    ["Recording and checking working time: employees must record working time using the fingerprint scanner or another method provided by the Company.", "Employees must check the accuracy of their working time approximately five days before payroll, following the procedures below."]
