  "8": [
    ["At a work location equipped with a Company fingerprint scanner, employees must scan in and out as evidence of actual attendance. The Company will send working-time information through the LINE application for employees to verify."],
    ["At a work location without a Company fingerprint scanner, the person responsible for attendance must prepare a working-time record instead of fingerprint records and post it for employees to verify."],
    ["If an employee finds an error in the working-time record, the employee must complete a time-correction form and submit it to the person responsible for attendance at that work location within three days after receiving the information through LINE or after it is posted. The correction must be completed before payday.", "If the employee does not submit a correction form, or submits it late, the record will be treated as checked and accepted for calculating wages, overtime pay, holiday work pay, holiday overtime pay and other employment benefits."],
    ["Holidays and rules for taking holidays."],
    ["Weekly holiday: the Company provides at least one weekly holiday. Sunday is treated as the weekly holiday."],
    ["Traditional holidays: the Company provides at least 13 paid traditional holidays per year, including National Labour Day, and announces them no later than December each year. If a traditional holiday falls on a weekly holiday, a substitute holiday will be provided on the next working day."],
    ["Annual vacation: an employee becomes entitled to six paid annual vacation days after completing one full year of continuous service.", "The employee must request permission at least one day in advance and receive supervisor approval before taking annual vacation. Taking leave without approval will be treated as absence and abandonment of duty.", "Annual vacation must be used within that year. It cannot be carried forward or exchanged for wages. Unused leave will be regarded as voluntarily waived by the employee, rather than a failure by the Company to provide the leave."],
    ["Overtime and holiday work: where the nature of the work requires continuity and stopping would cause damage, or in an emergency, a supervisor may issue a written order for necessary overtime, holiday work or holiday overtime. The employee's prior consent is required. Payment will follow the rules in Chapter 3."]
