  "10": [
    ["Wages", "Wages mean the base salary paid by the Company under an employment contract or another written agreement as compensation for the employee's work. Wage calculations are based on the actual facts.", "If an employee does not report for work and the absence is not valid leave or a valid holiday under Company regulations and procedures, the Company will treat it as absence or abandonment of duty and will not pay wages for the day not worked.", "For this clause, the term wages is not intended as the statutory definition of wages under labour law."],
    ["Starting wage rates are determined by considering the nature of the work, ability, education, position, duties and individual responsibility.", "The rate will not be lower than the minimum wage or basic minimum wage required by the labour-protection law in force."],
    ["Wage adjustment and effective date", "When an employee is proposed for promotion to a higher grade or position carrying greater responsibility or importance, a wage adjustment may be considered as appropriate.", "The adjustment must pass the written HR evaluation process and receive supervisor approval at least 15 days in advance. An approved adjustment takes effect on the 16th day of the relevant month."],
    ["Overtime pay and holiday work pay."],
    ["Overtime work and calculation", "The Company classifies overtime work as follows."],
    ["Overtime on a normal working day is paid at not less than 1.5 times the employee's normal hourly wage for each hour worked beyond normal working hours. This applies to monthly-paid and daily-paid employees."],
    ["Overtime on a holiday is paid at not less than three times the employee's normal hourly wage for each hour worked beyond the normal hours applicable to that workday. This applies to monthly-paid and daily-paid employees."],
    ["Holiday work and calculation are classified as follows."],
    ["For a monthly-paid employee working on a weekly holiday, the Company pays an additional amount of not less than one times the normal hourly wage for the hours worked on that weekly holiday, because normal pay for the weekly holiday is already included as required by labour-protection law."]
  ],
  "11": [
    ["For a daily-paid employee working on a weekly holiday, the Company pays not less than two times the normal hourly wage for the hours worked on that weekly holiday, because the employee does not ordinarily receive wages for the weekly holiday."],
    ["Work on a traditional holiday or annual vacation day is paid at not less than one additional times the normal hourly wage for the hours worked. This applies to both monthly-paid and daily-paid employees because their ordinary pay for those paid holidays is already provided.", "Employees authorised to act independently and conclusively on behalf of the Company in hiring, merit awards or termination, as specified in the delegation-of-authority manual, are not entitled to overtime or holiday work pay where the law excludes their position.", "Employees assigned to any of the following work are not entitled to overtime or holiday overtime, but may receive compensation equal to the normal hourly wage for the hours worked or holiday work pay where applicable.", "Work performed away from Company premises where the nature or circumstances of the work do not allow the working period to be clearly fixed.", "Watch or property-guarding duties assigned to employees whose regular duties are not security work.", "Work involving security or the guarding of Company premises or property.", "Other work prescribed by Company procedures."],
    ["Deductions from salary, overtime pay, holiday work pay and holiday overtime pay.", "The Company has no policy of making deductions except in the following cases and only at rates consistent with labour-protection law."],
