  "13": [
    ["Sick leave."],
    ["An employee may take sick leave for as long as the employee is actually ill and will receive wages for no more than 30 days per year. An employee unable to work because of illness must notify the supervisor immediately or without delay by any available method. On the first day back at work, the employee must complete the Company's sick-leave form and submit it to the supervisor that day."],
    ["For sick leave of three working days or more, the employee must provide a certificate from a first-class medical practitioner or a government medical facility. If the certificate cannot be produced, the employee must explain the reason to the supervisor, who may make enquiries or contact the treating facility and determine the appropriate leave period."],
    ["Claiming sick leave without actually being ill will be treated as intentional abandonment of duty, dishonesty toward the Company and serious misconduct."],
    ["If an employee on sick leave has recovered, the Company may direct the employee to return to work before the period stated in the medical certificate expires."],
    ["Where continuing illness causes an employee to use more than 30 normal working days of sick leave in a calendar year, the Company may adjust the employee's work, duties or position to suit the employee's physical condition and operational needs without unfairly reducing basic rights. If continuous illness prevents work for more than 90 normal working days, the Company may follow the applicable legal process and may consider termination on the ground that the employee cannot normally perform the work. Statutory severance and benefits, if any, will be paid fully and fairly."],
    ["Sterilisation leave."],
    ["Male and female employees have equal entitlement to sterilisation leave. The employee must submit a leave form and medical appointment evidence to the supervisor at least three working days in advance. Leave may be taken only after written approval and this entitlement may be used only once."],
    ["The period of sterilisation leave is the period prescribed and certified by a first-class medical practitioner."],
    ["The employee will receive wages for the medically certified period and must submit the supporting evidence to the Company within seven working days after returning to normal work."],
    ["Sterilisation leave that does not comply with these regulations will be treated, as applicable, as absence or abandonment of duty or work."]
  ],
  "14": [
    ["Maternity leave", "The Company permits maternity leave under the following rules."],
    ["A pregnant employee may take maternity leave, including prenatal examination leave, for no more than 120 days per pregnancy. Pay during maternity leave is provided subject to the paid-leave limit stated in these regulations and applicable law."],
    ["To take leave in preparation for childbirth, the employee must submit a leave form, notify the supervisor and request approval. The supervisor may consider the facts and may consult the physician at a medical facility contracted by the Company to examine, diagnose and determine an appropriate maternity-leave date."],
    ["If an emergency childbirth makes it impossible to request leave that day, the employee or a family member must notify the supervisor at the first available opportunity without delay."],
    ["Holidays occurring during maternity leave are included in the leave period."],
    ["For the safety and health of a pregnant employee, if a first-class medical practitioner certifies that the employee cannot continue her original duties because they may affect the pregnancy, the Company may temporarily assign suitable work before or after childbirth at the discretion of HR and under Company procedures."],
    ["The Company does not permit a pregnant employee to perform work that may affect the pregnancy, health or safety."],
    ["After childbirth, the employee must submit evidence of the birth to the Company within seven days after returning to normal work."],
    ["Maternity leave that does not comply with these requirements will be treated, as applicable, as absence or abandonment of duty or work."],
    ["A pregnant employee, or an employee who becomes aware of the pregnancy, should immediately notify the supervisor using the Company's pregnancy-notification form so the Company can provide appropriate treatment and arrangements. If concealment or failure to notify causes an inadvertent breach of labour law, the Company will be regarded as having acted without knowledge in good faith."],
    ["For additional safety and health protection, a pregnant employee may not drive or travel on unsafe vehicles, work between 22:00 and 06:00, work overtime or work on holidays. A pregnant employee in management, professional, administrative, finance or accounting work may perform necessary overtime on a normal working day where it does not affect her health, subject to applicable requirements."]
  ],
  "15": [
    ["Continuous childcare leave", "The Company permits continuous childcare leave under the following rules."],
    ["After using maternity leave, a female employee may take up to 15 additional days per pregnancy to care for a child where a qualifying condition genuinely exists. Pay is one-half of the normal hourly wage for the leave period, up to 15 days."],
    ["Continuous childcare leave may begin only after maternity leave has been fully used, so the entitlements do not overlap. It may be taken continuously or otherwise as permitted. Leave is counted in calendar days, not working days, and holidays or other leave occurring during the period cannot be excluded to extend the entitlement."],
    ["The employee must submit a leave form, notify the supervisor and request approval supported by a diagnosis from a first-class medical practitioner. A qualifying condition includes a risk of complications, abnormality or disability of the child. A medical certificate and clear medical evidence confirming the diagnosis must be provided for the Company to decide whether to approve the leave."],
    ["Holidays occurring during continuous childcare leave are included in the leave period."],
    ["If the qualifying condition is diagnosed after maternity leave has ended, continuous childcare leave may still be requested regardless of the interval, provided the diagnosed qualifying condition from that pregnancy still exists. An unrelated later illness is not a qualifying condition."],
    ["Continuous childcare leave may be approved only once for each pregnancy, and the qualifying condition must genuinely exist."],
    ["The Company may issue procedures defining qualifying conditions as necessary and appropriate."]
  ],
  "16": [
    ["If the employee has not obtained and cannot provide a certificate from a first-class medical practitioner, continuous childcare leave will not be approved. While a qualifying condition exists, the employee may instead request personal leave or annual vacation according to the available entitlement."],
    ["After completing continuous childcare leave, the employee must return to work for the Company within three normal working days."],
    ["Failure to comply with the rules for continuous childcare leave will be treated, as applicable, as absence or abandonment of duty or work. Dishonest use of the entitlement may also result in disciplinary action."],
    ["Leave to assist a spouse after childbirth", "The Company permits leave to assist a spouse after childbirth under the following rules."],
