  "23": [
    ["Scope and meaning", "A dispute exists where a conflict arises concerning an employee's work or conduct. An employee involved in the dispute may submit a grievance using the following procedure and investigation process."],
    ["The grievance must be in writing and describe the details and circumstances of the dispute, including its time, place and persons involved."],
    ["The requested determination must be stated. The complainant must provide the complainant's full name and sign personally."],
    ["The complainant must first submit the grievance to the department manager. If there is a reason this cannot be done, it may be submitted to the next level of supervision."],
    ["After receiving a grievance, the department manager must consider, investigate and determine it, and notify the complainant of the decision within 30 days from receipt."],
    ["Appeal and final grievance process", "If the department manager's decision is unsatisfactory, the employee may submit a written appeal with an explanation to a Senior Manager, General Manager or Managing Director. The appeal decision and reasons must be communicated within 30 days from receipt. The decision at that level is final. If the complainant accepts the result at any stage, the matter ends at that stage."],
    ["Protection of complainants and related persons", "Throughout the grievance, investigation, decision and resolution process, the Company assures that a good-faith grievance and good-faith cooperation as a witness will not affect the work of the complainant or related persons. The matter is confidential. Unauthorised disclosure is misconduct and may result in disciplinary action."],
    ["The Company reserves the right to amend, change, supplement or cancel these regulations and human-resource management procedures as appropriate. Where the Company or an authorised person prescribes otherwise for a particular case, that direction shall be followed."]
  ],
  "24": [
    ["Resignation: an employee of any category wishing to resign must give the Company written advance notice as follows."],
    ["Management-level employees: at least 90 days."],
    ["Employees below management level: at least 30 days. A resigning employee is entitled to wages through the last day of employment and other benefits under Company rules."],
    ["Retirement: employment ends when the employee reaches 55 years of age. After retirement, the Company may consider continued employment individually where appropriate."],
    ["Termination without employee fault and severance pay: where the Company can no longer retain an employee for reasons such as reduced capability, health, economic conditions or restructuring, and the employee has committed no disciplinary offence, severance will be paid as follows."],
    ["Continuous service of at least 120 days but less than one year: not less than 30 days of the last wage rate."],
